  "question": {
    "text": "Two long current carrying conductors are placed parallel to each other at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> between them. The magnitude of magnetic field produced at mid-point between the two conductors due to current flowing in them is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;T</mi></math>. The equal current flowing in the two conductors is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "R6n1S",
      "text": "&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> in the same direction.<br />&nbsp;",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ri5ra",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> in the opposite direction.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kZqAr",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;in the opposite direction.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hCfgF",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> in the opposite direction.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4752c0f6-4e4e-480a-b0d2-ddd73affa0a1-image.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>Magnetic field in parallel wires is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>At midway,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>distance</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>I</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>08</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>08</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;so&nbsp;the wires are carrying current in opposite direction. &nbsp;</p>",
